<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Shenzhi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">862–925</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Shenzhi was the founder of the state of Min in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>. He came south with his brother's rebel army and ruled Fujian from 898, receiving the title Prince of Min in 909 from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/later-liang">Later Liang</a>. He promoted overseas trade at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanzhou">Quanzhou</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a> and kept peace with his neighbours. His sons later took the title of emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-shenzhi.jpg" alt="Wang Shenzhi" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LuHungnguong · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uong_Sing-di.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
